From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:44:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Partition every initial grid, including same-level
 siblings

The nested-grid partition walk in InitializeNew descended only the
first-child chain (NextGridNextLevel) and skipped partitioning any
grid with a sibling, so with several nested grids on one level the
extra patches were never partitioned or visited. Snapshot the
initial-grid list with a full hierarchy traversal before partitioning
(CommunicationPartitionGrid splices new siblings into the chains), then
partition each entry. The non-nested path keeps its old behavior of
partitioning only the top grid.
---
 src/enzo/InitializeNew.C | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 48 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/enzo/InitializeNew.C b/src/enzo/InitializeNew.C
index 00e12be..8b5632b 100644
--- a/src/enzo/InitializeNew.C
+++ b/src/enzo/InitializeNew.C
@@ -260,12 +260,32 @@ int GetUnits(float *DensityUnits, float *LengthUnits,
 
  
 // Character strings
